// Precedence: a project-local Silver module beats a custom native name.
// `dupmod.sr` (same directory, listed in `sources`) defines `dupFn` as plain
// Silver; the manifest also declares a custom `dupmod` with fake files. The
// bare line must resolve to the Silver file (no fake dll emitted); the
// dormant custom grant is harmless (calls resolve user-first, lazily).
import { dupFn } from dupmod;

int precedenceHelper(int x) {
    return dupFn(x);
}
